31:["$","section","How to Convert GPA to CGPA?",{"children":[["$","h2",null,{"children":"How to Convert GPA to CGPA?"}],[["$","p","To compute CGPA, students need sum their total grades from all semesters in that subject.",{"children":"To compute CGPA, students need sum their total grades from all semesters in that subject."}],["$","p","Students should divide their final grade by the number of courses they attended, i.e. credit hours.",{"children":"Students should divide their final grade by the number of courses they attended, i.e. credit hours."}],["$","p","Students must add the figures that will finish and indicate the final CGPA achieved by a student in a course or in a class after subtracting the CGPA of each topic.",{"children":"Students must add the figures that will finish and indicate the final CGPA achieved by a student in a course or in a class after subtracting the CGPA of each topic."}],["$","p","The Central Board of Secondary Education stated in 2017 that the 10th Board results will be in the form of CGPA rather than percentage.",{"children":"The Central Board of Secondary Education stated in 2017 that the 10th Board results will be in the form of CGPA rather than percentage."}],["$","p","The CGPA can only be in even numbers. For instance: 8, 8.2, 8.4, 8.6, 8.8, 9….",{"children":"The CGPA can only be in even numbers. For instance: 8, 8.2, 8.4, 8.6, 8.8, 9…."}],["$","p","What is CGPA?",{"children":"What is CGPA?"}],["$","p","The Cumulative Grade Point Average (CGPA) is an abbreviation for the Cumulative Grade Point Average. The CGPA is the average of a student’s grade point average across all courses, except the sixth extra subject. The Central Board of Secondary Education released the CBSE Class 10 and 12 results in the form of CGPA. The CGPS is also noted on the students’ report cards.",{"children":"The Cumulative Grade Point Average (CGPA) is an abbreviation for the Cumulative Grade Point Average. The CGPA is the average of a student’s grade point average across all courses, except the sixth extra subject. The Central Board of Secondary Education released the CBSE Class 10 and 12 results in the form of CGPA. The CGPS is also noted on the students’ report cards."}],["$","p","If a student wishes to know how much of a % they received on the board test, they must convert their CGPA to Percentage. We have discussed in detail how to compute the CGPA and % from the CGPA Grades. Knowing the percentage will also assist pupils get admission to college and advance in their careers. Class 10 and 12 percentages are essential in the interview and shortlisting process.",{"children":"If a student wishes to know how much of a % they received on the board test, they must convert their CGPA to Percentage. We have discussed in detail how to compute the CGPA and % from the CGPA Grades. Knowing the percentage will also assist pupils get admission to college and advance in their careers. Class 10 and 12 percentages are essential in the interview and shortlisting process."}]],["$","ul",null,{"children":[]}]]}]
32:["$","section","What is the Importance of GPA and CGPA?",{"children":[["$","h2",null,{"children":"What is the Importance of GPA and CGPA?"}],[["$","p","Both GPA and CGPA are important, and they are linked to one another.",{"children":"Both GPA and CGPA are important, and they are linked to one another."}],["$","p","GPA is used to calculate CGPA for a topic. Students must get high GPA scores in order to achieve a higher CGPA, since CGPA is determined by adding all semester results, while GPA is obtained from a single semester.",{"children":"GPA is used to calculate CGPA for a topic. Students must get high GPA scores in order to achieve a higher CGPA, since CGPA is determined by adding all semester results, while GPA is obtained from a single semester."}],["$","p","A high GPA and CGPA is required for admission to the world’s most prestigious institutions. Some important things to remember are:",{"children":"A high GPA and CGPA is required for admission to the world’s most prestigious institutions. Some important things to remember are:"}],["$","p","GPA should be maintained in order to get a high CGPA.",{"children":"GPA should be maintained in order to get a high CGPA."}],["$","p","During the admissions process, colleges want a student’s CGPA and GPA.",{"children":"During the admissions process, colleges want a student’s CGPA and GPA."}],["$","p","CGPA and GPA are required for different scholarship programmes.",{"children":"CGPA and GPA are required for different scholarship programmes."}],["$","p","A good CGPA and GPA are required to apply for placements.",{"children":"A good CGPA and GPA are required to apply for placements."}],["$","p","CGPA and GPA are also required for higher education programmes.",{"children":"CGPA and GPA are also required for higher education programmes."}]],["$","ul",null,{"children":[]}]]}]
